1
00:00:00,630 --> 00:00:02,580
- [birds chirping]
- [ALDARP] So...

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:06,210
you just brazenly show up
at my abode, is that the deal?

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,380
Well, yeah,
but very reluctantly.

4
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:09,790
Unbelievable.

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,710
It's like you have
a fatal allergy

6
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,040
to staying outta trouble.

7
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,960
I guess I'm stuck
helping you out,

8
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,830
but I don't ever
wanna hear you whining

9
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:17,830
about me anymore!

10
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,040
Because you're just
as bad, Kazuma!

11
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,710
He certainly is!

12
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,170
So, he can hardly refer to us

13
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:25,420
as "troublemakers"
anymore now, can he?

14
00:00:25,790 --> 00:00:26,960
Of course, as his friends,

15
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,460
we'd still much rather
help him out

16
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,210
than leave him
to his own devices! -[graons]

17
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,130
Well, if it isn't the demented
little wizard girl.

18
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:35,380
You'd better not be planning
to blow away

19
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:37,380
my valuable property
as you did before.

20
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:38,580
Excuse me?

21
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:40,250
[grunts]
That said,

22
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:44,330
I do feel somewhat insulted
that the unsavory rumors

23
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:45,920
people have been
spreading about me

24
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
are being so easily believed.

25
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:51,630
Th-This is only one aspect
of the ongoing investigation.

26
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:55,500
[ALDARP] Oh! Of course.
I understand, Lady Dustiness.

27
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:58,380
You, at least,
are welcome to stay

28
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,460
- as long as you desire.
- Huh.

29
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:02,420
You heard him!
He said we can stay here

30
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,210
- as long as we want to!
- [ALL] Huh.

31
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:06,710
I get the biggest guest room,
you guys! Ha ha!

32
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:08,250
That's not fair, Kazuma!

33
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:10,500
I want the one closest
to the dining room!

34
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:11,630
[MEGUMIN] I would be best
suited to... -Hey,

35
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:12,580
- wait just a--
- ...the room with the highest

36
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:13,750
altitude possible!

37
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:16,540
Damn it, Aqua! Who told ya
you could come up here?!

38
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,290
- I am truly sorry.
- [whimpering]

39
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:19,630
Forgive them.

40
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:21,130
[whimpering]

41
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:23,250
You certainly seem
to have your hands full,

42
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:24,500
Lady Dustiness.

43
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,750
I apologize.

44
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,330
- [indistinct chatter]
- I'm so sorry.

45
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,750
So sorry!

46
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,000
[KAZUMA]
My plans have definitely taken

47
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,250
a strange twist.

48
00:03:03,790 --> 00:03:06,080
Man, I wish I was back
in that castle.

49
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:08,830
But, your big brother's
gonna try, Iris!

50
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,960
If a thief's coming,
I bet it'll be at night.

51
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:15,210
Huh?
What's that room?

52
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:20,330
[laughing]
[door closes]

53
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:22,000
[gasps] Oh, it's you.

54
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:23,670
- [KAZUMA] I'm Kazuma.
- Nothing of note in here.

55
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:25,130
I wouldn't just wander around

56
00:03:25,210 --> 00:03:26,750
unless you have
a very good reason.

57
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,210
[gasps]

58
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:29,790
- Whatcha lookin' at?
- Wait!

59
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,790
Hmm.

60
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,210
[humming]

61
00:03:34,330 --> 00:03:35,460
[KAZUMA]
The baths?

62
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:37,880
Is this a magic mirror?

63
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,380
Making sure
it's in good condition

64
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:42,250
since Darkness is here, huh?

65
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:45,170
So, so, would you care
to accompany me?

66
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:48,170
Obviously, I won't be swayed
by your wicked ways.

67
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:49,880
Now, go on and get outta here.

68
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,250
I'm using this room.

69
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:52,580
Ugh!

70
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,710
[gasps] What do you mean,
you're going to be using it.

71
00:03:56,790 --> 00:03:57,830
Come on, man,

72
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,960
quit thinkin' like
you're some kinda deviant.

73
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,330
I'm gonna sleep in this room

74
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:03,000
to keep my friends
from getting' creeped on!

75
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,040
Don't try it!

76
00:04:04,170 --> 00:04:06,040
I cannot allow
a rapscallion like you

77
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:08,250
to gaze upon
Lalatina's nubile body!

78
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:09,710
I really hate
to break it to ya,

79
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:12,080
but I've already been in
the bath with Darkness before!

80
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,080
Do you want me to let
the whole mansion know

81
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,420
what you've got in this room?

82
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,880
Time for us to make a deal.

83
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,210
If you don't want your
entire maid staff pissed off,

84
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:20,710
- keep your mouth shut!
- Huh.

85
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:22,540
Being constantly harassed

86
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:24,500
is just part
of a maid's job description!

87
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,580
I should be the one
who's making you an offer.

88
00:04:26,670 --> 00:04:29,250
I'm not exactly sure why,
but I get the distinct feeling

89
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:30,920
that you and I
are birds of a feather.

90
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,670
Why not choose
the much friendlier option?

91
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,080
Ba-dump! Ba-dump!

92
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,500
[DARKNESS] That is quite
an interesting offer.

93
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:41,580
In fact, perhaps you should
go over the terms for us.

94
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:44,250
♪

95
00:04:44,330 --> 00:04:46,210
[BOTH] This pervert
was trying to look in on...

96
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:48,670
- [thumps]
- [both gasps]

97
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,250
[KAZUMA]
I'm sorry.

98
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:54,250
It's been three days
since we got here.

99
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:56,500
Mansion life
is comfortable enough.

100
00:04:56,750 --> 00:04:59,130
But there hasn't really
been much happening so far.

101
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:03,830
♪

102
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,670
[munching]

103
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,080
Hm.

104
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:09,460
Hey, are you eating
your lunch now, Kazuma?

105
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:11,290
- Yeah. Good morning.
- Hm?

106
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:13,960
Actually,
it's the afternoon already.

107
00:05:14,330 --> 00:05:15,750
Listen, I was awake all night

108
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:17,170
keepin' a lookout
for the thief,

109
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,250
thank you very much!

110
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,960
Besides,
if what I heard is true,

111
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,920
you were stayin' up late
just about every night

112
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,960
- while I was away from Axel.
- [gasps]

113
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:26,670
Somebody told you that, huh?

114
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:29,290
You were taken so suddenly,
I was getting really worried!

115
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:30,830
But more importantly,

116
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,960
have you found any signs
of the thief, yet?

117
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,790
What got you so anxious?

118
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,080
You were seriously worried
about me, huh?

119
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,330
Guess that's pretty cute.

120
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:40,830
It-It's only because you
always manage to get yourself

121
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:43,210
into more trouble,
despite being such a weakling!

122
00:05:43,290 --> 00:05:44,830
You die at the drop
of a hat, too!

123
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,170
Hey, it's not as if I try
to get into trouble!

124
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,830
Just like I wasn't dying
on purpose either, all right?

125
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:50,830
Hm.

126
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,080
[KAZUMA] Oh, feels like
I'm living in a rom-com!

127
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:54,880
Oh, man, are you serious?

128
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:55,920
How am I supposed to react

129
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
when you're being so friggin'
sweet all of a sudden?

130
00:05:58,580 --> 00:05:59,750
- [MEGUMIN] Kazuma.
- [gasps]

131
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,420
When you're finished
eating your meal,

132
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,630
would you like
to join me for a date?

133
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:06,330
Ba-dump!

134
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:10,170
♪

135
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:12,210
[MEGUMIN]
Explosion!

136
00:06:12,290 --> 00:06:15,290
[explosion]

137
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,630
- Huh.
- How did I know

138
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,170
it'd be somethin' like this?

139
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:24,290
[gulping]

140
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:26,330
- [exhales]
- [gasps]

141
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:27,920
[MEGUMIN]
Plosion!

142
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:29,460
[explosion]

143
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:31,670
What's that?
The Devil King Army?

144
00:06:31,790 --> 00:06:34,790
[all laughing]

145
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:38,750
- [MEGUMIN] Sion!
- [explosion]

146
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:41,830
[people shrieking]

147
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:44,880
[KAZUMA] You know
the capital's already gettin'

148
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:46,750
a lot of complaints
about you, right?

149
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,460
[MEGUMIN] My name has begun
to resound, is that it?

150
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:51,290
[KAZUMA] Maybe
I should've just had you learn

151
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,960
advanced magic after all.

152
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,710
[MEGUMIN] I don't
appreciate that, Kazuma!

153
00:06:54,830 --> 00:06:56,080
Not one little bit!

154
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,630
[KAZUMA]
So, after that.

155
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,580
[AQUA]
Hey, do you think you can screw

156
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:01,250
with a hardcore water Goddess?

157
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,380
[KAZUMA] Aqua spent
the entire week drinking up

158
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,330
all of the best booze
in the mansion.

159
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:09,630
Well, it was then
that my Explosion magic

160
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:12,500
burst forth laying waste
to the despicable general

161
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:14,420
of the Devil King's army, Hans!

162
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,880
Then came the time I battled
another general, Sylvia.

163
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:19,130
[KAZUMA] Megumin
regaled us daily, at length,

164
00:07:19,210 --> 00:07:20,960
about her heroic triumphs.

165
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,500
And, as for me...

166
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:26,170
Excuse me, Miss,
I think it's about that time.

167
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,750
- Could I get my usual massage?
- Huh.

168
00:07:27,830 --> 00:07:28,880
And, for dinner tonight,

169
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:30,880
can we have
giant beef sukiyaki?

170
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,920
Also, the down blanket
should be coming in soon,

171
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,250
just put it on my bed.

172
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:36,630
[ALDARP]
Uh, my dear Lady Dustiness.

173
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:37,670
[gasps]

174
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:38,790
[ALDARP] I, uh...

175
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,040
I do realize I said
to make yourself

176
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:42,420
at home, but perhaps I...

177
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,540
You do not need
to finish the thought!

178
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:46,670
We will leave
as soon as possible.

179
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:48,210
[crickets chirping]

180
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:50,500
[KAZUMA]
I slept so much this afternoon

181
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:52,040
that I'm wide awake, now.

182
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:53,830
Midnight snack time.

183
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,420
[sighs]

184
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,630
Totally sucks that
we're leaving tomorrow.

185
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,000
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

186
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,130
Is that Aqua?

187
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:03,540
[CHRIS]
There aren't any guards.

188
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,330
Maybe I'm being paranoid?

189
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:08,710
[gasps] Yes!
It's my last night here

190
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:10,130
and I'm hitting the jackpot!

191
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:12,830
Thank you so much, Eris,
the Goddess of luck!

192
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:13,880
[CHRIS]
Hm?

193
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:16,460
I'm feeling the weirdest
presence all of a sudden.

194
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:17,790
[KAZUMA]
Lurk.

195
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,330
- [CHRIS] Guess it's nothing.
- Dat, dat, dat, dat, dat, da.

196
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,000
[CHRIS]
So, Detect Treasure says

197
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,380
what I'm looking for
should be over this way.

198
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,130
Pounce! Gotcha!

199
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,380
[Chris screams]

200
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:30,630
[KAZUMA] Time to come along
quietly, you jerk!

201
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:32,210
You picked
the wrong mansion to rob!

202
00:08:32,290 --> 00:08:33,330
And you're not
dealing with some

203
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:34,960
two-bit
security guard, either!

204
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,830
I've taken down
Devil King generals,

205
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,710
so there's no way

206
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:39,210
you're gonna escape
this place! -[CHRIS] Stop it!

207
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,790
Wait a minute, are you?

208
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[KAZUMA]
Hang on,

209
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,210
where have I heard
that voice before?

210
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:45,960
[CHRIS]
Hey, is that you, Kazuma?

211
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,330
Listen, you really
need to watch

212
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:48,540
where you're
putting your hands!

213
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:52,210
I'm only restraining
a trespasser, that's all.

214
00:08:52,290 --> 00:08:53,580
It's me, okay?

215
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,460
[Chris sobbing]

216
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,130
Chris is the noble thief
they were talking about.

217
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:00,750
Who'll marry me now?

218
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:02,080
Well, what did you expect?

219
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:03,500
I thought
you were stealing stuff!

220
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:05,330
I don't understand, Kazuma!

221
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,830
What are you even doing here?

222
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:09,460
What?
So, Darkness is also here?

223
00:09:09,830 --> 00:09:11,290
That's bad! Very bad!

224
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,460
She's gonna be so mad
if she finds out!

225
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:15,460
There's a pretty good chance
they won't kill you

226
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,920
if you just apologize.

227
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,460
Pay your debt to society.

228
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:19,580
But you've got it all wrong!

229
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,960
I'm doing this for a perfectly
good reason!

230
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:24,380
[both gasp]

231
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:28,000
He didn't hear us.

232
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,130
Well, I suppose
I owe you an explanation.

233
00:09:30,210 --> 00:09:32,040
- So, I'll tell you the truth.
- Hm?

234
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,460
- It started way--
- Stop,

235
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:35,000
- I don't wanna know!
- And why not?

236
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,710
'Cause this is how I get
dragged into trouble

237
00:09:36,790 --> 00:09:37,750
every single time!

238
00:09:37,830 --> 00:09:38,920
Yeah but, still...

239
00:09:39,210 --> 00:09:40,250
Uh, whatever!

240
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:41,460
Your secret's safe with me!

241
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:42,880
Right now, you've gotta
hurry up and leave!

242
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,210
Fine, but I could
use your help.

243
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:45,580
I was kind of hoping you--
Huh. -Hmm.

244
00:09:45,670 --> 00:09:47,080
I do not wanna hear it!

245
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,250
Besides, think about it!

246
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,580
You know as well as I do
that the lord of this place

247
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:52,040
is a real pervert, right?

248
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:54,290
If he sees you've been
captured, then look out.

249
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:55,500
[gasps]

250
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:56,920
[DARKNESS]
I think I heard something.

251
00:09:57,250 --> 00:09:58,960
I-I'll head out
for tonight, then!

252
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,880
I can explain everything
some another time.

253
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:02,500
Don't even bother!

254
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:04,920
Wait, you oughta tie me up
before you take off!

255
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,960
That way I can just
tell 'em you escaped!

256
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,000
O-Okay! Now Bind!

257
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:10,330
- [groaning]
- See ya!

258
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,420
[thuds]

259
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,210
[groaning]

260
00:10:13,290 --> 00:10:14,670
Kazuma! Are you all right?

261
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,790
- Were you just hit with Bind?
- Where's the thief?

262
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:19,460
I hate to say it,

263
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:21,630
but right at the last second,
they got away.

264
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,130
Man, I was careless!

265
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:24,960
Could one of you
please untie me?

266
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:26,580
They have escaped then,

267
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,210
so are you injured?

268
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:29,670
What did the thief look like?

269
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,000
Uh, it, uh...

270
00:10:31,290 --> 00:10:33,790
It was a guy wearing
a weird-looking mask, I think.

271
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,500
And he might've
been even tougher

272
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,040
than a Devil King general, too.

273
00:10:37,290 --> 00:10:39,710
N-No way. He was that fearsome?

274
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,500
That must've been rough, then.

275
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:43,250
You sure are wrapped up tight.

276
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:44,920
Can you even move
at all right now?

277
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:46,460
What do you think?

278
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:47,670
It's too bad 'cause I had him

279
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:49,170
right where I
wanted him, but...

280
00:10:49,330 --> 00:10:51,080
Ah, just hurry and untie me.

281
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,290
This sucks.

282
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:53,290
Hmm?

283
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:55,460
- Huh.
- [AQUA] Uh, Kazuma.

284
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:57,880
This might not be
the best time to say it,

285
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,750
but I owe you a huge apology.

286
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,920
Am I missing something here?

287
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,210
Yeah, well, um...

288
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:05,380
So, you know how you
never came back again

289
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,790
after Princess Iris took you
away to the castle?

290
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,250
[KAZUMA]
Huh? Yeah.

291
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:11,710
I started randomly
digging around in your room

292
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:13,250
because I was really bored.

293
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:14,670
And then, I...

294
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:17,000
I found a doll-looking thingie
you must've made

295
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,580
and I accidentally broke it.

296
00:11:18,670 --> 00:11:19,920
You little...

297
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,210
That's fine!
Don't worry. I can fix it.

298
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:24,670
Now, if you'll untie me.

299
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,210
That's it? You forgive me?

300
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:27,670
Guess I might as well
clear the air

301
00:11:27,750 --> 00:11:28,920
while I've got the chance.

302
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,210
There, in your bedroom,

303
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:32,380
I figured it would be okay
since you weren't around,

304
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:34,000
so I started downing
some booze.

305
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,630
Truth is when I was drinking,

306
00:11:35,710 --> 00:11:37,500
cleaning up snack crumbs
and empty bottles

307
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,920
just seemed like a real pain.

308
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,580
So I just got hammered

309
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:42,830
and ended up breaking
a lot of other stuff, too.

310
00:11:44,250 --> 00:11:45,830
Sorry about that!
[chuckles]

311
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,580
[KAZUMA]
I could strangle her!

312
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,460
N-No problem!
'Cause we're good friends!

313
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,420
And I am the one who
didn't come back home.

314
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,040
Now, if you could just
untie me, then that would be...

315
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,380
- Huh?
- You know.

316
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:59,420
Regarding
this particular situation,

317
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,080
Aqua does have a valid point.

318
00:12:01,210 --> 00:12:04,130
I have a sneaking suspicion
that we're in for some fun.

319
00:12:04,210 --> 00:12:05,880
[gasps]

320
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,750
Hey, what's going on here?
[gasps]

321
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,540
- Please help me!
- Go on, then!

322
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:14,420
Say you regret being
such a cocky bastard lately!

323
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:17,540
Apologize for the endless grief
you have put me through!

324
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:19,630
"I am so sorry
for humiliating you!"

325
00:12:19,710 --> 00:12:21,040
- Say it! Now!
- I'm sorry!

326
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:23,500
I'm sorry
for causing you trouble!

327
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:25,710
Not a bad try,
but I need to hear you

328
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:27,080
say that again, Kazuma!

329
00:12:27,170 --> 00:12:28,250
You remember what you said!

330
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,750
Come on,
how many points was it?

331
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:32,580
Exactly how many points
does my Explosion magic get?

332
00:12:32,670 --> 00:12:34,710
You've gotta stop! The reason
you remember that stuff

333
00:12:34,790 --> 00:12:36,040
- is 'cause it's been said once!
- Oh, no,

334
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,670
go on and say it!
Don't be shy!

335
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:40,000
Just spit it out!
What are you waiting for?

336
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,290
Come on!

337
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,250
[DARKNESS] I had no idea
that turning the tables

338
00:12:43,330 --> 00:12:44,540
could be so fun!

339
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:47,290
How do you like it? Huh? Huh?

340
00:12:48,830 --> 00:12:50,630
♪

341
00:12:50,710 --> 00:12:51,670
[RAIN]
I see.

342
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:54,170
Despite all of your
confident assertions,

343
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:55,880
you still failed the task.

344
00:12:56,250 --> 00:12:58,250
You said "The thief wore a mask

345
00:12:58,330 --> 00:13:00,380
and was extremely
formidable," right?

346
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,790
Yeah, that's right!

347
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,420
But I wouldn't say the whole
thing was a total failure!

348
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,290
'Cause, if I hadn't been there,

349
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:08,580
who knows what would've
happened to old man Aldarp?

350
00:13:08,670 --> 00:13:09,960
He was worthless.

351
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,130
Indeed,
quite a worthless adventurer.

352
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:13,210
[gasps]

353
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:14,290
[sighs]

354
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:16,670
Sir Kazuma has
courageously battled

355
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:18,330
the Devil King's generals.

356
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,420
So, I'm quite certain

357
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:22,420
this thief must've been
a serious threat.

358
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:23,790
Hold on, Kazuma--

359
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:25,420
[gasps]
Huh.

360
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,500
Huh.

361
00:13:27,830 --> 00:13:28,830
I see.

362
00:13:29,630 --> 00:13:31,750
Well, in any event,
I must thank you.

363
00:13:32,170 --> 00:13:35,000
Rather than failing
to apprehend the devious thief,

364
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:37,960
you successfully stopped him
from stealing anything.

365
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:41,630
So, in my eyes you've done
nothing to earn derision.

366
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:43,290
[gasps]

367
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:47,710
You should be grateful
for Princess Iris' mercy.

368
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:50,080
But that said,
there's no reason for you

369
00:13:50,170 --> 00:13:51,540
to remain in the castle.

370
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:53,170
Forthwith, take your leave.

371
00:13:53,250 --> 00:13:54,250
Huh.

372
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:56,170
Hm.

373
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:59,920
♪

374
00:14:00,210 --> 00:14:01,670
The bubbly around the capital

375
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:03,460
sure doesn't live up
to all the hype.

376
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:05,250
Souvenir shopping, huh?

377
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:07,420
How insensitive
can one person be?

378
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,880
I'm pretty depressed here.

379
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,130
It's not like we have
anything else to do, right?

380
00:14:11,210 --> 00:14:12,250
You little!

381
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,330
I can't find
anything round here.

382
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:16,250
Michael from Axel
has way better stuff

383
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:17,670
in his store, to be honest.

384
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,960
So, who the hell
is this Michael guy?

385
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,210
You've turned into a real
"social butterfly"

386
00:14:22,290 --> 00:14:23,380
back home, haven't you?

387
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:26,170
Just the other day,
some guy came by the mansion

388
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:27,790
and left a bunch
of expensive meat

389
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,540
to thank you
for healing him up.

390
00:14:29,710 --> 00:14:32,460
[gasps] Wait,
nobody said anything to me

391
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:35,420
and I don't remember getting
any meat! So, where did it go?

392
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,080
Simple, Darkness cooked it
and then we both ate--

393
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:40,420
Excuse me?
And I didn't get one bite?

394
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,380
You've got a lot of explaining
to do, you know that? -Oh, Aqua

395
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:44,500
what a coincidence
running into you out here!

396
00:14:45,290 --> 00:14:46,330
[KAZUMA]
Huh?

397
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:49,330
♪

398
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:50,380
Who are you?

399
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,380
It seems you still have

400
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,250
a wonderful sense
of humor, Aqua.

401
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:54,750
Okay, this guy is being

402
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:56,540
a little too familiar
and it's so weird.

403
00:14:56,630 --> 00:14:58,420
Hi, it's, uh, it's me.

404
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,750
The Sword Master you
granted the cursed sword to

405
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:01,790
some time ago.

406
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:03,880
It's Katsuragi!
You remember him, don't ya?

407
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,750
I told you
My name's Mitsurugi!

408
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,290
It's Mitsurugi!

409
00:15:08,330 --> 00:15:09,960
[KAZUMA] Guess it'll take
more than his name.

410
00:15:10,210 --> 00:15:11,290
He's got the cursed sword.

411
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:13,170
- Remember that?
- Yeah.

412
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:15,750
Come on, you didn't actually
forget my name, did you?

413
00:15:16,170 --> 00:15:18,380
Why don't you say the whole
thing, just to make sure?

414
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:20,080
I mean, I could do that,

415
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:21,790
but it feels like you're
putting me on the spot.

416
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:24,210
It's Kyouya! If you've
forgotten, then just admit it!

417
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,250
My name is Kyouya Mitsurugi!

418
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:27,420
[sighs]

419
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:28,960
Whatever.

420
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:31,290
- But, more importantly, Aqua.
- [AQUA] Huh.

421
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:35,380
[MITSURUGI] I'd like to express
my gratitude for our reunion.

422
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:37,880
- What, for me?
- Hm.

423
00:15:39,670 --> 00:15:42,250
It's just something that
I picked up during my travels.

424
00:15:42,830 --> 00:15:45,210
Though, I'm not confident
you like this sort of thing.

425
00:15:46,130 --> 00:15:47,920
[KAZUMA]
Oh, isn't he such a gentleman?

426
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,170
What a move!
I am so pissed off!

427
00:15:51,130 --> 00:15:52,130
Hm.

428
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:54,710
This ring's way too small
for my finger.

429
00:15:55,210 --> 00:15:56,500
[Mitsurugi groans]

430
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,710
[MITSURUGI] Could I get three
glasses of bubbly, please?

431
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:04,790
♪

432
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,330
[snoring]

433
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:07,420
[CHRIS]
Wake up.

434
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,130
Come on, wake up already.

435
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,830
[groaning]

436
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:16,790
- Come on, Kazu--
- Intruder!

437
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:18,080
[Chris screams]

438
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:20,250
[CHRIS]
Hey, it's only me, okay?

439
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:22,500
Cut it out!
Whoa, don't touch me there!

440
00:16:22,630 --> 00:16:24,170
Darkness! Darkness! Help!

441
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:25,460
[KAZUMA]
Oh, it's you, Chris.

442
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:26,920
Who did you think it was?

443
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:28,460
Now, tell me the truth!

444
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:30,080
When you sprang out of bed
and jumped on me,

445
00:16:30,170 --> 00:16:31,210
did you know I was?

446
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:33,580
First, you roll up in
a guy's room for a booty call,

447
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:36,040
then scream when you get
touched? Is this a honey trap?

448
00:16:36,130 --> 00:16:38,130
It wasn't a booty call
or a honey trap!

449
00:16:38,210 --> 00:16:40,040
I already told you that
I was gonna come by here

450
00:16:40,130 --> 00:16:42,000
and explain, so that's
exactly what I did!

451
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,710
- Hmm.
- [CHRIS] Hang on!

452
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:45,750
Don't suddenly pretend
you can't hear me!

453
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,630
I thought I already told you
I didn't wanna hear it!

454
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:49,830
You should try
coming back later!

455
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:51,670
Like, oh, I don't know,
next year, maybe?

456
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:53,290
But I've gotta
handle this, now!

457
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,500
Come on,
just hear me out! Please?

458
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:58,540
Please, please, please,
please, please, please, please.

459
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,250
Okay, damn it! Go ahead!

460
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:02,330
For some time,
I've been gathering

461
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:04,380
these incredibly powerful
and rare items

462
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:05,670
called Divine Treasures.

463
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:07,210
Huh, Divine Treasures?

464
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:09,420
Sounds like trouble,
so can we stop now?

465
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:10,420
Just listen!

466
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,880
These items are normally
only given to adventurers

467
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,750
with dark hair, dark eyes,
and funny-sounding names.

468
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,420
Really weird ones
just like yours.

469
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,540
Don't call my name weird. Hm?

470
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,130
[KAZUMA] The reincarnated
people get cheat items

471
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:23,420
when they show up here.

472
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,000
Is that what she's looking for?

473
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,630
Each one of them
has different effects.

474
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:29,630
Some can do
a whole lot of damage,

475
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:31,790
while others can bring
incredible wealth.

476
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:34,790
Wealth?
[gasps]

477
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:35,920
Huh.

478
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:39,250
[gasps]

479
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:41,670
♪

480
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,540
- That was you?
- Listen, I'm sorry, okay?

481
00:17:44,630 --> 00:17:46,750
But they're more dangerous
than you can even imagine!

482
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:48,500
So, they all need
to be gathered up!

483
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:49,960
By who and what for?

484
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,210
Well, I, uh...

485
00:17:51,290 --> 00:17:53,420
My client says that
I'm not allowed to share

486
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,830
any of the details.

487
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,540
- I don't care, then!
- [screams]

488
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:58,330
But this is
the most important part!

489
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:00,580
I can sense the presence
of an amazing treasure

490
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:01,830
coming from the castle!

491
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:02,960
You've gotta be kidding me!

492
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,750
That's the most obvious thing
you could've said!

493
00:18:04,830 --> 00:18:06,080
Yep! And, with that in mind,

494
00:18:06,170 --> 00:18:07,420
I wanted to ask you
for some help.

495
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:10,250
I knew it! I'm through
getting mixed up in bad news!

496
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:11,380
[gasps]

497
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,130
You have the Night Vision
skill, don't you?

498
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,880
Along with Lurk
and Enemy Detection?

499
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,380
Couldn't you use those to try
and help me out a little bit?

500
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:19,500
Stop trying to turn me
into a criminal!

501
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:21,130
Man, I was right
about all this!

502
00:18:21,210 --> 00:18:22,750
There is no way
I'm gonna help you!

503
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:23,830
So, you might
as well forget it!

504
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:26,540
Ah, come on! Don't be
like that, you big meanie!

505
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:29,080
Get out! You better get
outta here right this minute!

506
00:18:29,170 --> 00:18:30,670
'Cause if you don't,
I'll use Bind

507
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:32,420
before harassing you sexually!

508
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,830
- Huh.
- [Kazuma groans]

509
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,170
[CHRIS] I'm gonna
head back for now.

510
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:38,500
We can talk more about
all this stuff tomorrow.

511
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:41,330
I told you to "quit it!"
Now, bye.

512
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,830
[gasps] All right, I'll let you
off the hook this time!

513
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,710
♪

514
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,580
[sighs]
Damn it.

515
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:52,710
Man, I wish
I could catch a break.

516
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:56,540
Ugh, Eris, you have my word.

517
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,710
When I finally
get back to Axel,

518
00:18:58,790 --> 00:19:00,500
then I'll convert
to your church,

519
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:01,960
so, until I get out there,

520
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:03,960
please grant me
a little peace and quiet.

521
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:05,170
Hmm.

522
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:08,380
[foghorn blaring]

523
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,080
[screams]

524
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:16,710
[ANNOUNCER 03-A (F)]
Devil King Army alert!

525
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:18,290
Devil King Army alert!

526
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:20,500
A group belonging
to the Devil King's army

527
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:22,170
has been deployed
near the capital!

528
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:23,750
All knights must be ready!

529
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:26,920
Any high-level adventurers
are now requested to assist!

530
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,790
- [knocking on door]
- Kazuma, hurry up!

531
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,250
Get your gear together.

532
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:31,710
[KAZUMA]
Can't, sleeping.

533
00:19:31,790 --> 00:19:33,420
This is not the time for jokes!

534
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,080
The Devil King's army is here!

535
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:36,920
So, every one of us needs
to join the fight!

536
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,710
Sounds like you're the one
joking to me!

537
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:40,920
You heard what she said
in the announcement, right?

538
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,380
They want
"High-level adventurers"

539
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,920
and I think we all know
I'm pretty "mid!"

540
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,080
Besides, isn't this whole city

541
00:19:45,170 --> 00:19:46,750
supposed to be crawling
with badasses?

542
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:48,630
I'm sure they can
handle it just fine!

543
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:51,130
You can be
such a coward sometimes!

544
00:19:51,210 --> 00:19:54,040
Suit yourself! I will take
Aqua and Megumin and go!

545
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:57,000
Keep trembling in bed,
you low-level adventurer!

546
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Hmph!

547
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:00,580
[door closes]

548
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:04,960
[AQUA] No, are you kidding?
That sounds too dangerous!

549
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,500
Why do I have to go?

550
00:20:06,630 --> 00:20:09,000
I only came to the capital
to goof around!

551
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,540
So, there is no way
I'm gonna fight

552
00:20:10,630 --> 00:20:11,630
against the Devil King's army!

553
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,540
You should stop
being so selfish, Aqua!

554
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:16,330
In these situations, you can
never have too many healers!

555
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:19,170
Just look at Megumin!
She is absolutely raring to go!

556
00:20:19,250 --> 00:20:21,250
Darkness,
I'm going ahead to confront

557
00:20:21,330 --> 00:20:22,750
- the Devil King's forces.
- [gasps]

558
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,710
If the battle starts
and different factions

559
00:20:24,790 --> 00:20:26,210
become tangled up in a melee,

560
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:28,580
then I won't even have
a chance to use my magic!

561
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:30,710
The very first strike
is going to be mine!

562
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:32,460
And I am betting
my powered-up magic

563
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:34,750
will both begin and end
the fighting all at once!

564
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:36,420
[Darkness groans]
Wait, Megumin!

565
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,630
Do not be so reckless!

566
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:38,920
And, Aqua, just give it up!

567
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,130
Oh, come on, Kazuma!

568
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:43,670
- I really need your help here!
- [screams]

569
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:45,460
Why are you guys
always screaming?

570
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:46,710
There's no reason to butt in

571
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:49,210
on something this dangerous
and risk our necks.

572
00:20:49,630 --> 00:20:52,330
[gasps]
Hey, hang on a minute.

573
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:54,880
If I can show off a little
during this thing,

574
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:56,040
then that might be
what it takes

575
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:57,500
to get me back in the castle.

576
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,130
I mean, there's already
a bunch of adventurers

577
00:21:00,210 --> 00:21:01,790
with tons of cheats
in the capital!

578
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:04,380
So I seriously doubt
the bad guys will win.

579
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,040
It's not like I need to head
out there and wipe the floor

580
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:09,380
with the Devil King's guys
all by myself.

581
00:21:10,130 --> 00:21:12,210
As long as I put on
a decent enough show,

582
00:21:12,290 --> 00:21:13,790
that oughta do the trick!

583
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,170
Enough, Darkness!

584
00:21:15,250 --> 00:21:17,790
I have a terribly bad feeling
about this!

585
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:20,330
You can have one of my
breakfast sausages, okay?

586
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:22,460
Let's put this on hold
till tomorrow!

587
00:21:22,670 --> 00:21:25,580
When the royal army finally
arrives out on the battlefield,

588
00:21:25,710 --> 00:21:27,130
they'll see
the smoldering remains

589
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:28,330
of the Devil King's forces,

590
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:30,500
and a wizard taking
her well-earned leave.

591
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,130
Yeah, that's what I wanna do!
And now's my big chance!

592
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:35,540
So, you've got to let me go
before it gets any later!

593
00:21:35,630 --> 00:21:39,500
Kazuma, I need your help!
Do something about these two!

594
00:21:39,630 --> 00:21:40,630
[both gasp]

595
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:44,880
Listen, Ladies,
the kingdom needs our help.

596
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:48,420
Off we go!

597
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,630
It's our turn to kick
some major butt!

598
00:21:51,630 --> 00:21:53,000
[whimpering]

599
00:21:53,130 --> 00:21:56,130
[screaming]
[wailing]

600
00:23:29,630 --> 00:23:32,630
[VERDIA]
Strike! Strike!

601
00:23:33,630 --> 00:23:35,380
Howdy!
The weather's great here.

602
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:36,710
It's me, Verdia!

603
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,880
Y'know, no matter
how many times I...

